From: Fathom <fathom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] x1000: h2boot: note which stock firmware is in the flash (Eros Q)

When it boots Linux from a Fathom card, h2boot reads the stock kernel's
uImage header in the flash (64 bytes at 0x300000, partition mtd2), and
writes its name and build time to /fathom/stock-version when they differ
from what's there ("name=Linux-3.10.14", "time=1762858730"). Linux can't
read the flash; Fathom's Uninstall uses the note to refuse a HiBy update
older than the firmware in the flash (an older U-Boot can leave the screen
blank on a newer H2). Each HiBy release builds its kernel within a minute
of its version.txt date.

The code is Fathom's bootloader/fathom/fwcopy.c (the header, tested on the
host by tests/test_fwcopy.c) and fwcopy-h2boot.c (the flash and the card).
---
--- a/bootloader/x1000/boot.c	2026-11-19 20:09:15
+++ b/bootloader/x1000/boot.c	2026-11-19 20:09:15
@@ -136,6 +136,8 @@
     /* Fathom: first, the Bluetooth and Wi-Fi firmware onto the card, from
      * the stock system in the flash, if it isn't there yet */
     fathom_copy_firmware(false);
+    /* Fathom: which stock firmware is in the flash, for Uninstall Fathom */
+    fathom_note_stock_version();
     show_boot_logo();   /* Fathom: on screen while the kernel loads */
     /* Fathom: an update's kernel gets two starts to reach the player, then
      * the one before it goes back in place (bootpick.c) */
--- a/bootloader/x1000/x1000bootloader.h	2026-11-19 20:09:15
+++ b/bootloader/x1000/x1000bootloader.h	2026-11-19 20:09:15
@@ -200,6 +200,7 @@
  * the flash onto the card (fwcopy-h2boot.c); asked: from the menu */
 void fathom_copy_firmware(bool asked);
 void fathom_copy_firmware_menu(void);
+void fathom_note_stock_version(void);
 #endif
 
 #endif /* __X1000BOOTLOADER_H__ */
